abstract:
We say that a PDE in a Riemannian manifold $M$ is geometric if,$\ $whenever $u$ is a solution of the PDE on a domain $Ω$ of $M$, the composition $u_ϕ:=u\circϕ$ is also solution on $ϕ^{-1}\left( Ωight) $, for any isometry $ϕ$ of $M.$ We prove that if $u\in C^{1}\left( \mathbb{H}^{n}ight) $ is a solution of a geometric PDE satisfying the comparison principle, where $\mathbb{H}^{n}$ is the hyperbolic space of constant sectional curvature $-1,$ $n\geq2,$ and if \[ \limsup_{Rightarrow\infty}\left( e^{R}\sup_{S_{R}}\left\Vert 
abla uight\Vert ight) =0, \] where $S_{R}$ is a geodesic sphere of $\mathbb{H}^{n}$ centered at fixed point $o\in\mathbb{H}^{n}$ with radius $R,$ then $u$ is constant. Moreover, given $C>0,$ there is a bounded non-constant harmonic function $v\in C^{\infty }\left( \mathbb{H}^{n}ight) $ such that \[ \lim_{Rightarrow\infty}\left( e^{R}\sup_{S_{R}}\left\Vert 
abla vight\Vert ight) =C. \] The first part of the above result is a consequence of a more general theorem proved in the paper which asserts that if $G$ is a non compact Lie group with a left invariant metric, $u\in C^{1}\left( Gight) $ a solution of a left invariant PDE (that is, if $v$ is a solution of the PDE on a domain $Ω$ of $G$, the composition $v_{g}:=v\circ L_{g}$ of $v$ with a left translation $L_{g}:Gightarrow G,$ $L_{g}\left( hight) =gh,$ is also solution on $L_{g}^{-1}\left( Ωight) $ for any $g\in G),$ the PDE satisfies the comparison principle and% \[ \limsup_{Rightarrow\infty}\left( \sup_{g\in B_{R}}\left\Vert \operatorname*{Ad}
olimits_{g}ight\Vert \sup_{S_{R}}\left\Vert 
abla uight\Vert ight) =0, \] where $\operatorname*{Ad}
olimits_{g}:\mathfrak{g}ightarrow\mathfrak{g}$ is the adjoint map of $G$ and $\mathfrak{g}$ the Lie algebra of $G,$ then $u$ is constant.
